Dropping 1 test patients with stage(s) unseen in training: Stage II
Test set for scoring: 147 patients

===== HELD-OUT TEST C-INDEX (the real comparison) =====
Plain clinical (age+gender+stage, PH-VIOLATED): test C=0.610
Stratified clinical (age+gender|stage, PH-valid): test C=0.495

===== DEPLOYMENT DECISION =====
Plain model wins on real held-out discrimination, but VIOLATES the PH assumption.
Deploying it anyway would mean shipping a statistically invalid model.
Decision: deploy the STRATIFIED model regardless — a lower but VALID C-index
is more defensible than a higher one from a model whose assumptions are known to be false.

FINAL DEPLOYMENT MODEL: stratified
Saved p4_model_selection.rds
